          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nThe patient has generalized epilepsy with generalized tonic-clonic seizures beginning at 6 years of age. The epilepsy has a genetic etiology due to a pathogenic PCDH19 variant, c.918G>A. The condition is drug responsive. Brain MRI demonstrated nonspecific white matter changes.\n\nCurrent Medication:\n- Oxcarbazepine, current antiseizure medication.\n\nSeizure Burden:\nApproximately 6 generalized tonic-clonic seizures per week.\n\nAssessment:\nGeneralized genetic epilepsy associated with PCDH19 c.918G>A, presenting with generalized tonic-clonic seizures. Drug-responsive status is noted. MRI shows nonspecific white matter changes.\n\nPlan:\n- Continue oxcarbazepine.\n- Continue monitoring seizure frequency.\n- Follow up in the epilepsy clinic.",
